Chunk: efficient breakdown of man-made polymers and the transformation of waste materials into useful compounds.   6  Conclusions  Enzyme biocatalysts present an environmentally friendly option for managing and recycling plastic waste. It is possible to incorporate enzyme-mediated biocatalytic degradation into existing plastic recycling frameworks, complementing or potentially replacing current chemical recycling methods. Modifying the active sites of enzymes is one potential strategy for improving the stability of plastic-degrading enzymes, allowing them to function in a broader range of environments. Additionally, engineering a single functional system suitable for more than two types of plastics broadens the spectrum of plastic degradability within a single test. New opportunities to obtain novel biocatalysts with ideal properties for efficient and cost-effective plastic depolymerization have emerged as a result of the rapid advancements in synthetic biology and protein engineering, which
